@startuml data-flow
!theme plain
title M5 — Event ingestion flow (user_event)

actor "Visitor"               as V
participant "Web (browser)"   as W
participant "FemiGlow API"    as API
participant "Stalwart SMTP"   as SMTP
participant "Listmonk"        as LM
database    "Postgres"        as DB

== Web tracking ==
V -> W : page view, click, add-to-cart…
W -> API : POST /api/tracking/events
API -> DB : INSERT user_event\n(event_name, properties, session_id, source='web')

== Order placed (server) ==
V -> API : POST /api/checkout/order
API -> DB : INSERT orders
API -> DB : INSERT user_event\n(event_name='order.placed', source='server')

== Email lifecycle ==
API -> SMTP : send mail
SMTP -> API : webhook delivery/bounce
API -> DB : UPDATE email_outbox\nINSERT email_event
API -> DB : INSERT user_event\n(event_name='email.delivered'\nor 'email.bounced',\nsource='email')

== Newsletter (Listmonk) ==
LM -> API : webhook subscriber.created\n/subscribed/bounced
API -> DB : UPDATE email_subscriber_link\nINSERT email_event
API -> DB : INSERT user_event\n(event_name='subscriber.created',\nsource='email')

== Admin action ==
note over API
  Quand un admin modifie un lead
  (status, note, tag…), on enregistre
  aussi en user_event pour la
  traçabilité audience.
end note
API -> DB : INSERT lead_events\nINSERT user_event\n(source='admin')

@enduml
